<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khiva</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khiva is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, long the capital of the Khanate of Khiva. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> campaigned against it in 1740 during his Central Asian expeditions. In the nineteenth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> reduced Khiva to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> as part of its expansion into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khiva.jpg" alt="Khiva" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fulvio Spada from Torino, Italy · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_from_the_city_walls,_Khiva_(4934484894).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1740 he campaigned in Central Asia, subduing Bukhara and <b>Khiva</b>, while keeping up military pressure on the Ottomans in the west, which ended in his victory at Kars in 1745.</blockquote><a href="/empire/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The subjugation of the Central Asian khanates of Bukhara (1868), <b>Khiva</b> (1873) and Kokand (1876) brought the frontier to the borders of Afghanistan and British India, and generated the 'Great Game' rivalry with Britain that governed Central Asian political geography until the Anglo-Russian Convention of 1907.</blockquote><a href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Uzbek tribes from north of the Aral Sea invaded in 1501, and before the Russians arrived the country was divided between the Emirate of Bukhara and the khanates of <b>Khiva</b> and Kokand.</blockquote><a href="/empire/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Wars with the Khanate of Kokand and <b>Khiva</b> were frequent.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-bukhara">Emirate of Bukhara</a></li><li><blockquote>The juz was nomadic, raiding and trading with Russia and <b>Khiva</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/junior-juz">Junior Juz</a></li><li><blockquote>The Arabshahid dynasty ruled at first from Urgench and later from <b>Khiva</b>, which became the capital in the 17th century as the Amu Darya changed course.</blockquote><a href="/state/khanate-of-khiva">Khanate of Khiva</a></li></ul></section>
